==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|fi||*nyyt}} (with irregular shortening of the vowel ''yy'' > ''y''), from {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*nügüt}}. Compare {{m|fi|nyky-}}, {{m|fi|nytten}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|nüüd}}, {{cog|olo|nügöi}}, {{cog|lud|nügü}}, {{cog|vep|nügüd'}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Adverb===
{{fi-adv|-}}

# [[now]] {{gl|at the present time}}
#: {{syn|fi|juuri|nytten|nytte}}
#: {{ux|fi|Olen '''nyt''' kotona.|I'm (at) home '''now'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} {{n-g|Used when understating, belittling, etc.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Ei tämä '''nyt''' kyllä ihan hyvin mennyt.|This didn't really go all that well, did it.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Se '''nyt''' on pikkuseikka.|That's just a detail.}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} {{n-g|With an imperative or request, used to emphasize, to suggest impatience, or a wish to move on, or plead, etc.; often with ''vain''/''vaan''}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tee '''nyt''' se ensin, niin katsotaan sitten.|'''Just''' do it first and we'll see after that.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tulisit '''nyt'''!|Please, please come!}}
#: {{ux|fi|Ole '''nyt''' vaan hiljaa.|Just be quiet, will you.}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} {{n-g|Used when talking about something that the speaker knows and feels the person being spoken to knows as well.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Kyllä minä '''nyt''' sinua rakastan.|(Oh come on), I do love you.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Kai minä '''nyt''' sen tiedän!|Surely you don't think I don't know that?}}

